<article class="env-lemma" id="6EDD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/6EDD">Lemma <span data-tag="6EDD">6.5.3.11</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos, let $U_{\bullet }$ be a hypercovering of $\calX $. Then the colimit $| U_{\bullet } |$ is $\infty $-connective. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We will prove that $\theta $ is $n$-connective for every $n \geq 0$. Let $V_{\bullet } = \cosk _{n+1} U_{\bullet }$, and let $u: U_{\bullet } \rightarrow V_{\bullet }$ be the adjunction map. Lemma <a href="/tag/DC4F" data-tag="DC4F">6.5.3.10</a> asserts that the induced map $|U_{\bullet }| \rightarrow |V_{\bullet }|$ is $n$-connective, and Lemma <a href="/tag/3A66" data-tag="3A66">6.5.3.9</a> asserts that $| V_{\bullet } |$ is a final object of $\calX $. It follows that $| U_{\bullet } | \in \calX $ is $n$-connective, as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>